ifa/issues/055 -- FA does not converge (final_pass=41, pass_limit_hit=1, 152 violations) on plcfrs's splitgrammar() table-building shape, reduced to 36 lines. Needs all seven of: a nested tuple unpack in the generator feeding the set, enumerate(), two dicts over the same pairs with SWAPPED key/value, an array("B") arity vector indexed by a Rule field, Rule as a class rather than a tuple, the yf == arraytoyf(...) round-trip comparison, and the zip() generator inside arraytoyf. This is the SECOND plcfrs repro: the first (dict_pair_swap_setdiff_nonconvergence.py) was fixed by PYC_ROUTECYCLE and passes; this one does not need the set difference at all. CPython prints 3, which the check file records, so this flips to PASS when the remaining plcfrs non-convergence is fixed.
